1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,225
I worked the night shift

2
00:00:01,225 --> 00:00:02,212
at a gas station for

3
00:00:02,212 --> 00:00:02,776
one summer.

4
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,573
I quit the night the

5
00:00:04,573 --> 00:00:06,124
man in the yellow raincoat

6
00:00:06,124 --> 00:00:06,756
came back.

7
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:09,151
Because by then, I knew

8
00:00:09,151 --> 00:00:10,477
what he really wanted.

9
00:00:11,383 --> 00:00:13,086
Bus thirteen.

10
00:00:13,086 --> 00:00:15,883
Tonight's passenger...

11
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:18,802
still smells like rain.

12
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,886
It was the summer before

13
00:00:20,886 --> 00:00:22,274
my second year of college,

14
00:00:22,274 --> 00:00:23,149
and I was broke.

15
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:24,904
So when a gas station

16
00:00:24,904 --> 00:00:26,197
two miles outside town

17
00:00:26,197 --> 00:00:27,715
offered twenty-two dollars

18
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:28,333
an hour...

19
00:00:28,513 --> 00:00:29,573
I didn't ask why.

20
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,557
The owner was an old

21
00:00:31,557 --> 00:00:32,566
man named Dale.

22
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:34,205
Flannel shirt, big beard,

23
00:00:34,205 --> 00:00:35,213
firm handshake.

24
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:36,297
You must be Mia.

25
00:00:36,297 --> 00:00:37,201
Come on in, kid.

